  },
  text = {
    [1] = "With the Weathered Relic in your bags, go back to Drak'thul and pick his first dialogue choice each time he speaks; the step ends once he only sends you away.",
    [2] = "Use the Dowser while on the platform. Stand with the grapple point behind you; the spike on your left holds the first rune, and the others follow clockwise. Swap the runes above the chest until they match, in four swaps at most.",
    [3] = "The Forging page lies deep inside the cave at the map marker.",
    [4] = "Pick up the Souls page from the platform at the map marker.",
    [5] = "A rune teleporter near the marker takes you up to the spot; the Binding page waits at its far side.",
    [6] = "Release the Feral Shadehound at the altar, then press the action buttons in the rune order your Crumbling Stele shows.",
    [7] = "Open the Immaculate Sac of Swog Treasures: it holds the Aquatic Shades, a toy to learn.",
    [8] = "Put on the Aquatic Shades (a toy), swim down to the Bubble Bath and keep dancing on its stage until the dancing debuff ends.",
    [9] = "With the Reshii Wraps equipped, step through the phase conduit; it takes you into Untethered Space.",
    [10] = "Hunt Hal'hadar Manatech near Manaforge Arcvein, on Normal difficulty, until one of them drops the Specimen Container Key; expect many kills.",
    [11] = "Open the Specimen Container inside the manaforge with the key, on Normal difficulty.",
    [12] = "Touch all sixteen motes. Each one counts once, and characters on one account may share the work. The moment the last one is taken, the Mote of Nasz'uro arrives in your bags; learn the pet from it. If it does not show up, log out and back in.",
    [13] = "Alliance: Arielle Snapflash in Stormwind wants three things for her camera quest: a Standard Scope (made by engineers, or bought), a Russet Belt from a cloth armor merchant, and an Iron Box out of a Weathered Supply Crate in the city (68.1, 66.9). She pays with the S.E.L.F.I.E. Camera.",
    [14] = "Horde: Vivica Starshot in Orgrimmar wants the same three things: a Standard Scope, a Russet Belt from a cloth armor merchant, and an Iron Box out of a Weathered Supply Crate in the city (63.9, 19.7). She pays with the S.E.L.F.I.E. Camera.",
    [15] = "Her next quest sends you to Yojamba Isle off northern Stranglethorn Vale: defeat the Crystal Spine Matriarch there for a Pristine Crystal Shard.",
    [16] = "Use the S.E.L.F.I.E. Lens Upgrade Kit to turn your camera into the S.E.L.F.I.E. Camera MkII, which holds the background filters you unlock next.",
    [17] = "In Antorus, the Burning Throne, take a picture of yourself with Argus the Unmaker using the MkII camera to unlock the Argus filter.",
    [18] = "In Firelands, take a picture of yourself with Ragnaros using the MkII camera to unlock the Firelands filter.",
    [19] = "In Icecrown Citadel, take a picture of yourself with the Lich King while the fight is under way, using the MkII camera, to unlock the Frostmourne filter.",
    [20] = "In Terrace of Endless Spring, stand close to the Sha of Fear and wait for its opening speech to end, then take a picture of yourself with it using the MkII camera to unlock the Sha filter.",
    [21] = "In the Bastion of Twilight, take a picture of yourself with Cho'gall using the MkII camera to unlock the Twilight filter.",
    [22] = "You need the Torch of Pyrreth, from the Secrets of Azeroth questline, in almost every step below. Get it first if it is not yet in your bags.",
    [23] = "Pick the Detective title, which you earn with the achievement Azeroth's Greatest Detective, then talk to the Dalaran Survivor in Dornogal to start the hunt for Ratts.",
    [24] = "Enter the Pillar-nest Vosh cave beside Faerin's Advance. A hole high on one wall, which you can climb up to, drops into a hidden tunnel, and Ratts is at the end of it. Speak to him to finish the quest and receive the Peculiar Gem. Bring the three notes first.",
    [25] = "Stand at the gate of the Karazhan Catacombs in Deadwind Pass with the Peculiar Key in your bags and use the Torch of Pyrreth; a way opens into the Ratts' Revenge scenario, where the felcycle sits among twelve pillars.",
    [26] = "Hold your Torch at each of the three places below until a stack of the buff The Light of Their Love appears. With three stacks the first pillar lights.",
    [27] = "Hold the Torch at the Humble Monument in the Northern Barrens until a stack of the buff appears.",
    [28] = "Hold the Torch beside Decimator Olgra in Maldraxxus until a stack of the buff appears.",
    [29] = "Hold the Torch beside Olgra in Nagrand on Draenor until a stack of the buff appears. Where she stands depends on your quest progress; her other spot is at 74.2, 37.5.",
    [30] = "Summon a Perky Pug wearing one of the costumes and pick up the Gift of N'Zoth from one of the eyes. At the Ny'alotha obelisk in the Vale of Eternal Blossoms, use /pray. The Battle for Azeroth N'Zoth story must be finished.",
    [31] = "Dress your Perky Pug in the Dogg-Saron costume, which Vashti sells, or the Yipp-Saron costume, which comes from Hallow's End.",
    [32] = "Use a Twitching Eyeball or All-Seeing Eyes to get the Gift of N'Zoth buff.",
    [33] = "Open the chamber door in the room beside the Red Button with the Key of Shadows.",
    [34] = "In that room, cast your fishing line into the bowl on the left-hand bookcase; a key comes up.",
    [35] = "The key unlocks the chest in the same room. Inside are the Starry-Eyed Goggles: keep them on from here, since the consoles only show through them.",
    [36] = "Solve all nine decryption consoles below; each sits beside a chest that pays out one Piece of Hate. Keep all nine pieces, a later trade needs them.",
    [37] = "At the console beside this chest enter 88224646, press Submit, then open the chest.",
    [38] = "At the console beside this chest enter 17112317, press Submit, then open the chest.",
    [39] = "At the console beside this chest enter 1533, 3457, 8265 or 10638, press Submit, then open the chest. The goggles reveal this console.",
    [40] = "At the console beside this chest enter 19019, press Submit, then open the chest.",
    [41] = "At the console beside this chest enter 5661, press Submit, then open the chest.",
    [42] = "At the console beside this chest enter 52233, press Submit, then open the chest.",
    [43] = "At the console beside this chest enter 51567, press Submit, then open the chest.",
    [44] = "At the console beside this chest enter 115, press Submit, then open the chest.",
    [45] = "Any Feeling Lucky slot machine along the felcycle room walls works; enter 777, 888 or 168. It pays a Piece of Hate only if you carry five different lucky things, items or buffs. Thirteen lucky sources exist and the list here is only part of them. Stormwind sells three of them, and Griftah in Dornogal two.",
    [46] = "Use the scroll inside Uther's Tomb in the Western Plaguelands. A Doomguard appears and four pieces of graffiti become visible; interact with every one of them while the demon lives.",
    [47] = "Speak to Zarhym, a rare skull spirit near the cave mouth in the Cavern of Lost Spirits on the Timeless Isle, to cross into the spirit realm.",
    [48] = "Further into the cavern, Jeremy Feasel waits for a pet battle. Your team must be three level 25 secret pets (Baa'l, Snowclaw Cub and Taptaf are one team; Nelthara, Spyragos and Wicker Pup also count). Win, then talk to him for the Golden Muffin.",
    [49] = "Use the Torch at each of the five altars in Zul'Gurub, in Northern Stranglethorn, to call its spirit, then give that spirit everything it asks for.",
    [50] = "For the Sin spirit: wear any sinstone back cosmetic, summon the pet Sinheart and use the toy Bondable Sinstone.",
    [51] = "For the Corruption spirit: wear the Cloak of Overwhelming Corruption or a cloak that looks like it, use /cower on it, summon a mount and a pet that have corrupted in their names, and use the toy Ring of Broken Promises or Accursed Tome of the Sargerei.",
    [52] = "For the Void spirit: wear the Cloak of the Black Void or a cloak that looks like it, use /smirk on it, summon the pet Lesser Voidcaller, Sir Shady Mrrgglton Junior or Voidwiggler, and use the toy Shadowy Disguise or Void Totem.",
    [53] = "For the Lust spirit: take off your armor and clothes, use /flirt on it, summon the pet Sister of Temptation, and use the toy Moroes' Famous Polish or Steamy Romance Novel Kit.",
    [54] = "For the Blood spirit: summon a mount and a pet that have blood in their names, and use the toy Throbbing Blood Orb.",
    [55] = "Once every spirit is content, the Chest of Acquisitions sits against the wall close to the Shadow altar, visible only through the goggles. Open it for the Ancient Shaman Blood.",
    [56] = "Buy the Fledgling Warden Owl pet from this vendor (it needs Revered with the Wardens) and learn it; the owl must be out in step 21.",
    [57] = "Take your owl pet out on the Isle of the Watchers in Azsuna and stay with it in the glow of an owl statue that is lit up, until you hear a chime and see a magnifying glass over yourself. Four different glows count: red, green, blue and purple. When your owl carries a white orb above its head, it is finished.",
    [58] = "Empower the owl at a statue glow of a colour you have not done yet.",
    [59] = "Empower the owl at a statue glow of a colour you have not done yet.",
    [60] = "Empower the owl at a statue glow of a colour you have not done yet.",
    [61] = "Empower the owl at a statue glow of a colour you have not done yet.",
    [62] = "Run Vault of the Wardens at any difficulty and keep the owl out until the final boss. In Cordana's arena, take Elune's light from the glowing sentry statue and carry it back to where the dungeon begins; a door opens there, and the Sentry Statue stands in the middle of the room behind it.",
    [63] = "Take the statue to the Vault of Mirrors and put it down on the central platform that precedes the final staircase to Glazer.",
    [64] = "A grid of five by five statues appears. Interacting with one sinks it and toggles four others, and every statue has to end up sunk. Plan the clicks with a solver. When it is solved, loot the Warden's Mirror from the treasure.",
    [65] = "At the Enigma Machine, insert the Ancient Shaman Blood and the Warden's Mirror, press Begin once, then Submit: a random number of rats appears. Count the rats in the catacombs, leaving out the Catacombs Rats, then kill rats of both kinds so none steps on a plate. The machine has three locks.",
    [66] = "For each lock, turn the rat count into a plate and a number of statues, set that many statues on that plate, then press Submit.",
    [67] = "Plates 1 to 4: high in the felcycle room (71.6, 20.1); just inside its entrance (68.5, 34.2); past the locked east gate, opened with the Relic of Crystal Connections (73.6, 43.0); the corridor facing the felcycle room (68.8, 50.9).",
    [68] = "Plates 5 to 7: the flooded dead end near the catacombs entrance (73.6, 65.3); the corridor leading to the cat room (60.2, 71.6); a corner of the room where you caught the key (47.8, 78.9).",
    [69] = "Return to the Pillar-nest Vosh tunnel where Ratts was. Through the goggles a faint platform shows high above; the Relic of Crystal Connections on the humming crystal lifts you up. Type 84847078 at its console, press Submit, then open the chest beside it for the Keys to Incognitro.",
    [70] = "This continues Ratts' Revenge after the felcycle. Keep the Torch of Pyrreth and the Starry-Eyed Goggles from the first part, and note that these pillars came with a later patch.",
    [71] = "Bring a Bubblefilled Flounder: buy one on the Auction House, or catch the secret fish in the Hissing Grotto dive bar in the Waking Shores. That fish shows only to ghosts, so jump off a cliff and look around; it returns about every 45 seconds. With the Aquatic Shades on you can target it while alive.",
    [72] = "Put the egg down at the Duck Family beside Papa's Feather in Valdrakken and loot the Tuskarr Dinner Bell. When the duck family is not around, clicking the feather summons them.",
    [73] = "To'no wanders the Forbidden Reach and shows up at one of nine possible spots, but stays hidden until you step very close. Pick the second chat option for the Oddsight Focus; the first option pays random loot.",
    [74] = "In a group, go to the marked spot in southeastern Suramar and use the Torch until it shows a ghost that drifts around unseen. A button for the orb then appears on your screen; press it fast, since the ghost keeps moving.",
    [75] = "Carry the orb to Golk the Rumble in the middle of Azsuna. Whoever holds the orb has to stay on the ground, with no jumping, swimming or fighting, and sparking enemies keep attacking the holder, so bring a group.",
    [76] = "Speak to Golk with the orb. Everyone close by receives a Spare Key and a Weathered Lockbox.",
    [77] = "Open the Weathered Lockbox to learn Ensemble: Fashion of the Fanatic Felcyclist.",
    [78] = "Optional extra: carry the Spare Key and wear both the goggles and the Oddsight Focus buffs, and a footlocker becomes visible at the heart of the clock room in the catacombs. The key opens it and reveals Ratts' Journal, Page 317.",
    [79] = "Optional, and only as part of a full 40 player raid: at the Divine Flame of Beledar in Hallowfall, a raid leader conducts a song of 25 parts while every other member performs the emotes assigned to them, aimed at the flame. Each singer needs the Gift of Oddsight, from their own Oddsight Focus or from a friend using one on them.",
    [80] = "You need water breathing and an aquatic mount, such as a Battle Turtle, Ottuk, Seahorse or Tidestallion. Atomized Salien Slime works well because it adds swim speed; a short questline in Azj-Kahet gives it. A Draenic Water Breathing Elixir, a Shimmerscale Diving Helmet, Aquatic Form, Touch of the Grave or Unending Breath also work.",
    [81] = "In Vashj'ir, go to the safe spot at the edge of the fatigue waters south of the Abyssal Depths and dive straight down from exactly there on your aquatic mount, nudging sideways a little to reset the fatigue. When the water turns from grey to dark blue, swim straight at the pearl that rests beside a submerged skeleton. Touch it by swimming into it; do not click it.",
    [82] = "The pearl carries you to the hidden Seat of Knowledge. If you have fewer than seventeen secrets, Jeremy Feasel there sets your Hearthstone to this version of the room.",
    [83] = "Once you have solved at least seventeen of the secrets shown here, talk to Anakron and choose I am ready. Only secrets you solved yourself count; Auction House purchases do not.",
    [84] = "The records on the left side of the stairs: Lost Obsidian Cache, Wicker Pup, Glimr, Tobias, Voidfire Deathcycle, Incognitro, Fashion of the Fanatic Felcyclist, and Leaders of Scholomance.",
    [85] = "The records on the right side of the stairs: Slime Serpent, Nazjatar Blood Serpent, Courage, Kosumoth the Hungering, Bound Shadehound, Riddler's Mind-Worm, Phoenix Wishwing, Gortham, and Sun Darter Hatchling.",
    [86] = "The records beside Anakron: Enlightened Hearthstone, Long-Forgotten Hippogryph, Wan'be's Buried Goods, Uuna's secret storyline, Xy Trustee's Gearglider, Baa'l, Waist of Time, Jenafur, Otto, Hand of Nilganihmaht, Mimiron's Jumpjets, Thrayir, Crimson Tidestallion, Sinrunner Blanchy, The Hivemind, and Lucid Nightmare.",
    [87] = "Reach Revered or better with The Tillers, then find the Lost Dog at the crossroads in the Heartland of the Valley of the Four Winds and take the quest Lost and Lonely. Turn it in with 20 Tasty T-Bones. Finishing it sends Dog to your Halfhill farm and rewards the Wooden Doghouse decor.",
    [88] = "Collect 20 Tasty T-Bone from the Skyrange Mushan in the Valley of the Four Winds.",
    [89] = "Build the Herb Garden in your Warlords of Draenor garrison; Dog then turns up beside it.",
    [90] = "Search the red cobblestone of the main streets of Dalaran in the Broken Isles for a Pebble. It is tiny and can lie in many spots, and the Auction House sells them as well.",
    [91] = "Take the Pebble to your garrison, find Dog by the Herb Garden and show it to him; never throw it at him. He then moves to the pet menagerie in Dalaran.",
    [92] = "In the Tranquil Strand on the Isle of Dorn, among the Dalaran ruins, click the half-buried dog bowl.",
    [93] = "Talk to Dog and choose to pet his head; he becomes your companion pet.",
    [94] = "Upstairs in Curiosities & Moore in Dalaran, read the Inconspicuous Note lying on the table.",
    [95] = "Inside Ulduar, reach XT-002 Deconstructor's room. Pull the lever in the northwest scrap corner, then light the big grid of lights so they draw a gear.",
    [96] = "In the Temple of Ahn'Qiraj, go past C'Thun's chamber to the side room with the Mind Larva on a table. Keep playing its brain game until it ends; a row of five brains does it.",
    [97] = "When the game is won, check the Mind Larva's table again: another Inconspicuous Note lies there. Read it.",
    [98] = "Wear the Shadoweave Mask itself (a transmog look of it does not count). In the Crumbling Depths of Deepholm, enter the Dark Fissure, read the Dingy Plaque behind the chair in the cave below, then interact with the Strange Skull that shows up on the seat.",
    [99] = "Another Inconspicuous Note is now on the ground before the chair. Read it.",
    [100] = "In Gnomeregan, find the ten numbered consoles near the Launch Bay and set them so they read 1222176597.",
    [101] = "In the abandoned house by Ash'theran in Val'sharah, use the Nightmare Tumor and untangle its lines until none of them cross.",
    [102] = "In Kun-Lai Summit, enter the Tomb of Secrets and use the urn at the back. In the Endless Halls, carry each of the five colored orbs, one at a time, to the rune of its color.",
    [103] = "Enter the Forgotten Crypt in Deadwind Pass and go down to the Pit of Criminals. Open Puzzler's Desire on the pile of bones to get the mount.",
    [104] = "In Dalaran's Legerdemain Lounge, read Page 9 on the bookcase in the first room, beside the painting.",
    [105] = "Twilight Grove in Duskwood: beside the moonwell stands a little table with Page 78 on it. Read it.",
    [106] = "Inside the Firelands raid, fight your way to Ragnaros' platform and read Page 161 at the back of its left side.",
    [107] = "In Uldum, ask Zidormi in Ramkahen for the Cataclysm version of the zone. Read Page 655 standing between two small trees near the coast, close to the Lost City of the Tol'vir.",
    [108] = "In Siege of Orgrimmar, reach the Sha of Pride; Page 845 lies in the back corner of his chamber, on the left as you enter. Getting to the raid needs the old version of the Vale of Eternal Blossoms.",
    [109] = "Inside the Well of Eternity dungeon, defeat the first two bosses and read Page 1127 at the foot of the stairs, beside a large stone divider.",
    [110] = "Near the Shado-Pan Monastery in Kun-Lai Summit, read Page 2351 at the base of a statue.",
    [111] = "Back in Uldum, still in the Cataclysm version, read Page 5555 at the foot of a statue in the group east of the Halls of Origination.",
    [112] = "On the Westfall coast, open the Gift of the Mind-Seekers lying in the wreck of a boat to get the mount.",
    [113] = "Buy the Talisman of True Treasure Tracking from Griftah in Shattrath and keep it equipped through every step that follows: only its wearer sees the four glowing clues behind him and what they lead to.",
    [114] = "In Skyreach, defeat High Sage Viryx and use the console behind her. Click its small glowing orb, then guide the sun with the orbs around it: right, up, down, up, right, right, up, left, down, up, left, down. A chest holding the Green Crystal Monocle appears on the console.",
    [115] = "The Stellar Refraction Device sits one floor below the elevator hall of Halls of Origination, past the first boss; the stairs are on the hall's north side. Click it, then click the refractors until every constellation shows one color; a chest holding the Yellow Crystal Monocle appears on the device.",
    [116] = "Get 50 Glittergill Glitter by buying from the fish vendors of Vashj'ir in this order; each purchase pays with the goods of the one before.",
    [117] = "Buy 500 Seashells from Sir Finley Mrrgglton, who keeps watch from a tower on a little island above the waves.",
    [118] = "Buy 100 Cavity-Free Great Shark Teeth from Volatile Violetscale, deep down in the Underlight Canyon.",
    [119] = "Buy 50 Razoreel Larvae from Manta Stargazer, by the Shimmering Grotto, just under the waves.",
    [120] = "Buy 250 Well-Fed Doctor Fish from Lil' Whaley, at the Ruins of Thelserai Temple, down by the bottom.",
    [121] = "Buy 10 Freshly Molted Crab Skins from Gloomy Bluefin, southwest of the Abyssal Breach, at the bottom.",
    [122] = "Buy 50 Glittergill Glitter from Ol' Fishbreath, in Gnaws' Boneyard, high up in the plankton.",
    [123] = "Get 40 Symbiotic Plankton the same way.",
    [124] = "Buy 80 Seashells from Sir Finley Mrrgglton.",
    [125] = "Buy 2 Giant Giant Toenail Clippings from Gloomy Bluefin.",
    [126] = "Buy 4 Makrura Eyes from Little Carp at Deepfin Ridge, down low.",
    [127] = "Buy 1 Accidentally-Severed Seahorse Fin from Volatile Violetscale.",
    [128] = "Buy 2 Shiny Sea Serpent Scales from Crimson Angerfish by Biel'aran Ridge, deep in the water.",
    [129] = "Buy 40 Symbiotic Plankton from Manta Stargazer.",
    [130] = "Bring the 50 Glittergill Glitter and 40 Symbiotic Plankton to Sir Finley Mrrgglton and buy 5 Scintillating Murloc Skin Lotion with them.",
    [131] = "Get 5 Potent Gastropod Gloop the same way.",
    [132] = "Buy 300 Seashells from Sir Finley Mrrgglton.",
    [133] = "Buy 30 Vantus Black Squid Ink from Ol' Fishbreath.",
    [134] = "Buy 30 Super Slick Eel Slime from The Blackfish in the southwest of the Abandoned Reef.",
    [135] = "Buy 3 Rock-Encrusted Whelk Shells from Volatile Violetscale.",
    [136] = "Buy 5 Potent Gastropod Gloop from Little Carp.",
    [137] = "Get 5 Captured Cavitation Bubbles the same way.",
    [138] = "Buy 1,500 Seashells from Sir Finley Mrrgglton.",
    [139] = "Buy 300 Very Pretty Coral from Lil' Whaley.",
    [140] = "Buy 100 Iridescent Shimmerray Skins from Ol' Fishbreath.",
    [141] = "Buy 20 Luxurous Luxscale Scales from Crimson Angerfish.",
    [142] = "Buy 5 Captured Cavitation Bubbles from The Blackfish.",
    [143] = "Hand the 5 lotions, 5 gloops and 5 bubbles to Sir Finley Mrrgglton for the Red Crystal Monocle.",
    [144] = "The rest takes a party of exactly five with War Mode set the same way for all. Four of them each wear a different color of monocle; one monocle each is enough. Everyone keeps the Talisman on.",
    [145] = "The four monocle wearers each find the Wild Withered in Suramar whose eye color matches their monocle; with it on, that withered turns hostile. Bring all four down to almost no health at the same moment.",
    [146] = "Red monocle: Rikei.",
    [147] = "Blue monocle: Blom'an.",
    [148] = "Green monocle: Giluzui.",
    [149] = "Yellow monocle: Yorilan.",
    [150] = "Meanwhile the fifth player waits upstairs in a house in Suramar, outside a room barred by four colored beams. While the withered cast Draw Energy the beams drop for a few seconds; once all four are down together, go in, click the Lost Cat Toy behind the pillows and note the exact damage it deals.",
    [151] = "In the Court of Stars, find Lady Chaton and her mana kittens. Write the damage as five digits, with zeros in front if needed, and pet each kitten until its Purring stacks match one digit, in this order: Mrs. Fluffymuffins, Shadow, Mew, Ash, Bella. Click the Ominous Orb that appears to be taken onward.",
    [152] = "Cross the floating platforms as a group: each holds one player and lights up others, and one disappears once nobody keeps it up. Take turns hopping until all five stand at the far door, which opens only with everyone beside it.",
    [153] = "Ride the Lightlocked Platform over the energy field. The game secretly makes one of you the driver, two adults and two children; it crosses only with the driver plus one adult, one child or two children. Find the driver by trying pairs, then ferry everyone across and gather at the door.",
    [154] = "In the last room, all five stand on the purple circles and channel at once, and The Hivemind lands in your bags. Only the four who did this last run with you can ride along; doing it again with another group changes who.",
    [155] = "Collect 20 Abyssal Fragments. They drop from creatures across Kul Tiras and Zandalar, and other players sell them at the auction house.",
    [156] = "Take the 20 fragments to the Altar of the Abyss, at the end of the cave behind the waterfall in Stormsong Valley, and use it to make the essence.",
    [157] = "Take the essence to the Abyssal Icon in Saltstone Mine, in northern Stormsong Valley, and use it there to call the Adherent of the Abyss.",
    [158] = "In Nazmir, read the note on the high ledge beside the central temple. You can fly up to it.",
    [159] = "On the Broken Shore, click the pale pebble on the small stone table next to Drak'thul.",
    [160] = "In Boralus, climb down from the raised dock with the Homing Copter, walk through the net and the seaweed into the cave, and click the pale pebble on its floor.",
    [161] = "In Zuldazar, find the cave behind Atal'Dazar (outside the dungeon) and click the pebble at the foot of the tree root against the left wall.",
    [162] = "In Drustvar, follow the cave behind the narrow waterfall to its end. The pebble is tucked into the carved figure's skull; click it.",
    [163] = "In Vol'dun, find the cave mouth below the tall thin tree and click the pebble behind a small rock.",
    [164] = "In Stormsong Valley, fight through the pirates in the cave hidden among trees and click the pebble in the wheelbarrow.",
    [165] = "North of Nazmir, out at sea, dive to the sunken ship. In the stained glass at its stern, a row of pebbles curves below a skull: click the second one from the left. You need faster swimming to get there before the fatigue.",
    [166] = "In Boralus, near the hedge maze, the cellar behind the large tree holds stacked crates and a barrel. The pebble is out of sight at the back of that barrel; click it.",
    [167] = "On a small Drustvar island, stay out of the cave and jump onto the boulder at its mouth. The pebble sits on top, partly under creepers; click it.",
    [168] = "In Tiragarde Sound, drop into the hidden cave in the ground, where Clatterbacks leap out at you, and click the pebble wedged beside a rock in the gore.",
    [169] = "In Tiragarde Sound, go to the back of the cave behind the waterfall. A scroll lies open on the floor and the pebble is under it: stand over it, look up steeply with the camera, and click.",
    [170] = "Off the Boralus coast, swim through the seaweed into the underwater cave, reach the little island and click the pebble under the red kelp.",
    [171] = "At the northernmost tip of Vol'dun, swim down to the underwater cave and click the pebble just inside, ignoring the others.",
    [172] = "In Frostfire Ridge, Baa'l is in the volcano near Kurgthuk the Merciless. Call out a fully upgraded Uuna; she wears him down, and then you beat him in a pet battle.",
    [173] = "In Drustvar, click the unlit torches around the Hexed Chest to unlock it, then open it for the Bundle of Wicker Sticks.",
    [174] = "In Drustvar, open the Ensorcelled Chest for the Miniature Stag Skull.",
    [175] = "In Drustvar, click the unlit torches around the Enchanted Chest to unlock it, then open it for the Wolf Pup Spine.",
    [176] = "In Drustvar, click the unlit torches around the Bespelled Chest to unlock it, then open it for the Spooky Incantation.",
    [177] = "Use the four pieces together: they make the Spooky Bundle of Sticks, the item that teaches the pet.",
    [178] = "Talk to Amara Lunastar in eastern Ashenvale and tell her you will keep an eye out for her cat.",
    [179] = "Go into Donni Anthania's house in Elwynn Forest and look at the Empty Dish. If it is not there, talk to Amara Lunastar again.",
    [180] = "Inside Return to Karazhan, pick up eight foods: two Juicy Drumsticks, two Marbled Steaks, two Fishy Bits, a Meaty Morsel and a Slathered Rib. They lie in the Banquet Hall and the Guest Chambers. Each one disappears from your bags five minutes after you take it.",
    [181] = "In the Opera Hall, face away from the stage and lay the eight foods on the floor tiles, starting beside the two small kibble piles on the left and moving right: Juicy Drumstick, Marbled Steak, Fishy Bits, Meaty Morsel, Marbled Steak, Slathered Rib, Juicy Drumstick, Fishy Bits. Foods on the floor disappear after five minutes.",
    [182] = "Once the last food is down, Amara's Wish plays and Jenafur shows up in the hall. Go to her and pet her; she joins your pets.",
    [183] = "Click the Bone Effigy in Scavenger's Boneyard, with the Call of the Devourer and the three bones in your bags, to call the Many-Faced Devourer. Once you have done this, you can call it again whenever you like.",
    [184] = "Defeat this enemy for Uuna's Doll, then learn Uuna from the doll. It can be tried once a day.",
    [185] = "Call Uuna out and give her a moment: she greets you with one of three lines.",
    [186] = "Type /whistle at Uuna to get her attention.",
    [187] = "Type /roar at Uuna. She runs away, so summon her again.",
    [188] = "Type /cry at Uuna. She tells you the dark keeps her from seeing you properly.",
    [189] = "Walk Uuna up to A'dal in Shattrath; the Naaru's radiance overwhelms her and she bolts.",
    [190] = "Lead Uuna to Lake Falathim in Ashenvale so she can stand in its moonlight.",
    [191] = "Bring Uuna to Nuu, whose house sits on a small floating island off the far southwest of Eredath. It takes two glider jumps to get there.",
    [192] = "Bring Uuna to the Blood Watch outpost on Bloodmyst Isle.",
    [193] = "Take Uuna to the small camp in Draenor's Shadowmoon Valley; she picks up a wreath of flowers from a seat by the fire.",
    [194] = "Stay with her until void tendrils rise out of the earth and seize her.",
    [195] = "She can't be summoned now. Get yourself killed, talk to a Spirit Healer about Uuna to be let into the spirit realm, then run back to your body.",
    [196] = "Open the Shadow Tear in the Emerald Dragonshrine in Dragonblight. In the spirit realm, use /cheer on Uuna and put a Cooking Fire down next to her. For three minutes, run at the Soul-Eaters to scatter them; when she clutches herself and weeps, use /hug.",
    [197] = "Take Uuna to the Gate of the Setting Sun in the Vale of Eternal Blossoms. Ask Zidormi at the Seat of Knowledge for the older Vale first.",
    [198] = "Take Uuna to the Nighthold in Suramar.",
    [199] = "Take Uuna anywhere in Dalaran in the Broken Isles; Krasus' Landing works.",
    [200] = "Take Uuna to Wyrmrest Temple in Dragonblight.",
    [201] = "Take Uuna to Nordrassil on Mount Hyjal.",
    [202] = "Take Uuna to Neverest Pinnacle in Kun-Lai Summit.",
    [203] = "Take Uuna to Blackrock Mountain in the Burning Steppes.",
    [204] = "Take Uuna to the Temple of Karabor in Draenor's Shadowmoon Valley.",
    [205] = "Use Deal: Cartel Ba (only one Deal can be used each week, so all three drops take three weeks), then enter Manaforge Omega on any difficulty. After the first boss, take the right-hand path to the edge of the platform beside the teleporter to the central ring and loot the dead drop.",
    [206] = "Use Deal: Cartel Zo, then go to Mana-Vent Aphis in Manaforge Omega while Forgeweaver Araz is still alive. Walk the pipe that runs round the wall to its far end and loot the dead drop.",
    [207] = "Use Deal: Cartel Om, then head into Manaforge Omega beyond Fractillus. The dead drop sits on a boulder behind the building there.",
    [208] = "On the iceberg in the south of Grizzly Hills, chase the Glimmerfin Scout away and pick up the scale it leaves; that starts the quest chain.",
    [209] = "Defeat the Scuttleclaw Skimmers and Scuttleclaw Sandshells below the iceberg until you carry 10 Meaty Crab Chunks.",
    [210] = "Win a pet battle against Trainer Grrglin on his iceberg; he fields three aquatic pets.",
    [211] = "A Dark Iron Brewer in the Grim Guzzler, inside Blackrock Depths, leaves a Dire Brew behind once you have kept talking to him until he collapses.",
    [212] = "Make sure you own the battle pet Perky Pug, a reward of the achievement Looking for Multitudes; you will need to summon it later.",
    [213] = "The fire barrier lets through anyone who has drunk a Major Fire Protection Potion.",
    [214] = "The prismatic barrier needs protection from every school: drink a Major Frost, Holy, Nature and Shadow Protection Potion and one of the two Major Arcane Protection Potions, then walk through.",
    [215] = "The Diligent Watcher only notices the living, so drink Noggenfogger Elixirs until you have become a skeleton before you pass it.",
    [216] = "Scotty's Lucky Coin turns you into a sprite small enough for the wall of vines on the right. A Water Stone lies in the water beyond; take it.",
    [217] = "Activate the Water Stone and carry it back to the blue barrier, which then lets you through.",
    [218] = "Only dwarves get past the Stone Watcher, so drink a Dire Brew before you walk by.",
    [219] = "Upstairs, the right-hand path ends at a see-through barrier; Ethereal Oil makes you ghostly enough to reach the Strange Stone behind it.",
    [220] = "The Strange Stone's hole is fist-shaped and wants someone bigger: use a Gordok Ogre Suit together with a Winterfall Firewater, then put your arm in. You gain the Sign of the Second.",
    [221] = "Head back to the gate and drink Pygmy Oil until you are small enough to pass, then follow the left-hand path to the Wisdom Cube.",
    [222] = "Stand at the Wisdom Cube with your Perky Pug out, dress the pug in the \"Little Princess\" Costume, then pick the option to rest your arm under the cube. You gain the Sign of the First.",
    [223] = "In the last room downstairs, read the Tarnished Plaque on the pillar at your right. Cancel your Winterfall Firewater buff, then use a Scroll of Intellect.",
    [224] = "Past the plaque the floor dips into a pool. Walk into the water there (no jumping or swimming), cross to the far side and loot the Oddly-Colored Egg.",
    [225] = "Visit Ve'nari at her refuge in the Maw. She shows as a hologram now, with a new line of dialogue to pick.",
    [226] = "Travel to the Creation Catalyst in Zereth Mortis, where her body lies, and examine it through the dialogue choice.",
    [227] = "A few days later a message from Ve'nari reaches your mailbox with the toy inside.",
    [228] = "Climb the hill to the Blacktalon Shadowclaw, throw a Sour Apple at it, then ride it up the mountain.",
    [229] = "Call Baa'l out of your battle pet collection, on the character who defeated him.",
    [230] = "Visit Zidormi to see the Arathi Highlands as they used to be; Grimmy's list of friends lies on a table in his house by the coast. Read it.",
    [231] = "Put on the four uncommon pieces named in the list (Windwool Hood, Deathsilk Shoulders, Netherweave Tunic, Frostwoven Leggings), speak to Grimmy and choose the answer that presents you as an old friend.",
    [232] = "Carry all four items to Aquinastrasz in the Twilight Highlands and use /slap on Aquinastrasz.",
    [233] = "Carry all four items to Karnum Marshweaver in Desolace and use /wave at him.",
    [234] = "Carry all four items to Noggra in Zul'drak and use /cheer at her.",
    [235] = "Carry all four items to the Stained Mug in Kun-Lai Summit and use /dance next to it.",
    [236] = "Visit Grimmy again; a new answer mentions the messages you sent to his enemies. Choose it.",
    [237] = "Outside, keep using the Rotten Potato until the stacking buff it gives you reads exactly 144.",
    [238] = "Back with Grimmy, ask him to judge your scent.",
    [239] = "Grimmy's Rusty Lockbox sits up the slope past his house; open it.",
    [240] = "Solve the clue A Preservationist: Preservationist Kathos in the Valdrakken inn starts it with a box and a lost chalice.",
    [241] = "Solve the clue Ceremonial Spear: carry a tuskarr spear from Kathos to the elders of the Azure Span and Dragonblight, then to a memorial in Borean Tundra.",
    [242] = "Solve the clue Thinking Cap: build the Tricked-Out Thinking Cap with Bobby Carlisle's notes, then follow its arrows around Valdrakken.",
    [243] = "Solve the clue An Inside Job?: search a locker in the Valdrakken inn and have the banner inside appraised.",
    [244] = "Solve the clue Torch of Pyrreth: pull the levers of the Life-Binder Conservatory to win the Torch of Pyrreth, then test it in Valdrakken.",
    [245] = "Solve the clue A Chilling Ascent: find a hidden tablet near Vakthros in the Azure Span with the Torch and the Thinking Cap.",
    [246] = "Solve the clue The Idol of Ohn'ahra: light four braziers in the Ohn'ahran Plains with the Torch to win the Idol of Ohn'ahra.",
    [247] = "Solve the clue Shifting Sands: piece together a tablet from fragments in the Shifting Sands of Thaldraszus.",
    [248] = "Solve the clue What's in a Mold?: track down an ancient key mold in the Ohn'ahran Plains for Weaponsmith Koref.",
    [249] = "Solve the clue Forging is Key: gather dust and flux in the Waking Shores and forge a titan key with Koref.",
    [250] = "Solve the clue A Proper Burial: carry a centaur burial banner past five markers of the Ohn'ahran Plains to its resting place.",
    [251] = "Solve the clue Kirin Tor Knowledge: find hidden tomes in the library of Karazhan.",
    [252] = "Solve the clue A Curious Orb: rebuild the Orb of Rathmus from three caves in Thaldraszus. It opens once Under Suspicion is solved.",
    [253] = "Solve the clue Under Suspicion: collect six suspicious notes around Valdrakken.",
    [254] = "Solve the clue The Race: race the thief through Tyrhold in Thaldraszus. It opens once A Curious Orb is solved.",
    [255] = "In the Roasted Ram inn in Valdrakken, take the quest Preserving Rarities from Preservationist Kathos, then speak to her again for A Mystery Box. The Holiday Enthusiast outside the bank has a short optional quest that sends you to her.",
    [256] = "Take the Golden Chalice to the Valdrakken bank and set it down among the heaps of gold coins inside.",
    [257] = "Take the quest Rise in Relic Theft from Preservationist Kathos in the Valdrakken inn; she hands you a Tuskarr Ceremonial Spear.",
    [258] = "Elder Poa in Iskaara, in the Azure Span, turns it into Shomko's Unyielding Spear.",
    [259] = "Optional: show the spear to Elder Ko'nani at Moa'ki Harbor in Dragonblight for a drawing of where it belongs.",
    [260] = "Take Shomko's Unyielding Spear to Shomko's Remembrance on the Coast of Echoes in Borean Tundra and set it at the memorial.",
    [261] = "A Crazed Looter can turn up by the memorial; defeating it gives a Looter's Purse.",
    [262] = "Talk to Bobby Carlisle in the Valdrakken inn and take A Secretive Contact; his notes list the three parts of the cap.",
    [263] = "Ask Erugosa in Valdrakken about Thunderspine Nests; she gives you her shopping list.",
    [264] = "Bring Erugosa five Apexis Asiago, five Thunderspine Tenders and five Latticed Stinkhorn, from food vendors, and she cooks ten Thunderspine Nests. Five nests bought at the Auction House also do.",
    [265] = "Defeat a Hungering Tyranha at Cascade's Edge, just south of Valdrakken, for a Fresh Tyranha.",
    [266] = "Shakey Flatlap sells the Crystal Ocular Lenses for 1,000 gold. Or kneel at the Odd Statue in the Valdrakken inn to reach the Dragon's Hoard and settle a tab there for about 346 gold, which also earns the lenses.",
    [267] = "Use the Thought Calculating Apparatus to fit the liner and the lenses into it; you get the Unfinished Thinking Cap.",
    [268] = "The Unfinished Thinking Cap starts a quest; take it to Fangli Hoot, who finishes it into the Tricked-Out Thinking Cap toy.",
    [269] = "Fangli then gives you The Tricked-Out Thinking Cap quest. Wear the cap and follow the arrows it shows from clue to clue around Valdrakken, eight in all, and solve the riddle at the end, then turn the quest in to Fangli.",
    [270] = "Bobby Carlisle in the Valdrakken inn starts An Inside Job?; take it to Fangli Hoot, who gives you Fangli's Note and a Copied Artifact Storage Key.",
    [271] = "Open the Preservationist's Locker on the upper floor of the Valdrakken inn with the copied key and take the Maruuk Burial Banner from it.",
    [272] = "Show the banner to \"Appraiser\" Sazsel Stickyfingers in Valdrakken; she gives you the quest Preservationist Cleared.",
    [273] = "Preservationist Cleared has you return the banner; once it is back, turn the quest in to Fangli Hoot.",
    [274] = "Optional: Tithris in the Valdrakken inn gives you a Preservationist's Dispatch that points to the Life-Binder Conservatory in the Waking Shores.",
    [275] = "Pull the three Ancient Levers around the Life-Binder Conservatory.",
    [276] = "Once the levers are pulled, take the Torch of Pyrreth from its hiding place in the Life-Binder Conservatory; it starts Artifact Secured.",
    [277] = "Bring Artifact Secured to Preservationist Kathos; you learn the Torch of Pyrreth toy.",
    [278] = "Kathos then asks you to try the torch out in the quest The Torch of Pyrreth; bring her the Field Glasses it turns up.",
    [279] = "Hold the Torch of Pyrreth beside the Enchanted Box hidden in Valdrakken to reveal Kathos' Field Glasses, and pick them up.",
    [280] = "Take A Chilling Ascent from Bobby Carlisle in the Valdrakken inn; he gives you The Clerk's Notes.",
    [281] = "At Vakthros in the Azure Span, go to the great tower door at the foot of the tower. Wear the Tricked-Out Thinking Cap there and reset its count to 0, 0, then follow it to 11, minus 2, where a pillar stands.",
    [282] = "Hold the Torch of Pyrreth at the pillar to bring out the Unveiled Tablet, then take a rubbing of it; the rubbing starts A Knowledgeable Descent.",
    [283] = "Tithris in the Valdrakken inn hands you Preservationist's Dispatch Two, which sends you to the Eternal Kurgans in the Ohn'ahran Plains.",
    [284] = "Hold the Torch of Pyrreth at the Ancient Incense Braziers of the Eternal Kurgans until each lights: the three outer ones in any order, then the last one.",
    [285] = "Light one of the three outer braziers: at 32.3, 67.9, at 31.0, 70.8 or at 35.2, 65.7.",
    [286] = "Light a second outer brazier.",
    [287] = "Light the third outer brazier.",
    [288] = "With the three outer braziers lit, light the last one. If the torch will not light a brazier, switch to another shard of the zone.",
    [289] = "The Idol of Ohn'ahra appears beside the last brazier; pick it up to start An Idol in Hand.",
    [290] = "Bring An Idol in Hand to Preservationist Kathos; you learn the Idol of Ohn'ahra toy.",
    [291] = "For her next quest, use the Idol to find three gems hidden in Valdrakken, then report back to Kathos.",
    [292] = "Search the Shifting Sands of Thaldraszus for three Time-Lost Fragments; they lie close together.",
    [293] = "The Incomplete Tablet starts Out of the Sands; bring it to Preservationist Kathos.",
    [294] = "Bobby Carlisle in the Valdrakken inn starts A Key Story, which sends you to Weaponsmith Koref at the Earth-Warder's Forge in the Obsidian Citadel; he gives you The Blacksmith and the Apprentice.",
    [295] = "In the ruins of the Sylvan Glade in the Ohn'ahran Plains, hold the Torch of Pyrreth near the stones until the Hastily Scrawled Stone shows, and read the coordinates written on it.",
    [296] = "Wear the Tricked-Out Thinking Cap and follow it to the stone's coordinates, where the Ancient Key Mold lies hidden. Take the Titan Key Mold from it; the mold starts A Titanic Mold.",
    [297] = "Bobby Carlisle in the Valdrakken inn starts Reforging a Legend; take it to Weaponsmith Koref, who gives you the Titan Key Materials List.",
    [298] = "Summon the Idol of Ohn'ahra around the Overflowing Rapids in the Waking Shores to make the tiny Rose Gold Dust visible, and pick up fifty.",
    [299] = "Collect eight Igneous Flux along the Waking Shores coast, where lava runs into the sea.",
    [300] = "At the Earth-Warder's Forge in the Obsidian Citadel, speak to Koref to begin A Key to Reforg(ing). Add the dust and the flux, infuse the key with the Torch of Pyrreth, then take the Reforged Titan Key from the forge.",
    [301] = "Hand the Reforged Titan Key to Koref to finish A Key to Reforg(ing); its reward is the Tyr's Titan Key ensemble.",
    [302] = "Take A Proper Burial from Preservationist Kathos in the Valdrakken inn; she gives you a Maruuk Burial Banner.",
    [303] = "Show the banner to Sansok Khan in the Ohn'ahran Plains; it becomes Ishtaar Rethon's Burial Banner.",
    [304] = "Jhara gives you The Path of Ishtaar Drawing, which shows the Ohn'ahra statue above the Shikaar Highlands.",
    [305] = "Find the five Aged Markers along Ishtaar's path across the Ohn'ahran Plains.",
    [306] = "The first marker stands in the Shikaar Highlands.",
    [307] = "The second is at the back of a cave by the Roaring Dragonsprings.",
    [308] = "For the third, wear the Tricked-Out Thinking Cap at the Windsong Rise altar, reset it to 0, 0 and follow it to minus 2, 5, at the cliff edge.",
    [309] = "The fourth is in the second room on the left inside a burial mound in the southwest of the Eternal Kurgans.",
    [310] = "The fifth is in the Deadsnare Caverns behind spider webs; burn them away with the Torch of Pyrreth.",
    [311] = "At the back of the Deadsnare Caverns, upstairs, set the banner on the Large Unmarked Stone Cairn.",
    [312] = "Bobby Carlisle in the Valdrakken inn starts A Special Book and gives you his Kirin Tor contact's note.",
    [313] = "Enter the old Karazhan raid in Deadwind Pass and defeat Moroes, the Opera Hall event and The Curator to open the way to the Guardian's Library.",
    [314] = "In the Guardian's Library, summon the Idol of Ohn'ahra to point out the three Ancient Tomes, and use the Tricked-Out Thinking Cap with the coordinates each one gives.",
    [315] = "Read the first Ancient Tome.",
    [316] = "Read the second Ancient Tome.",
    [317] = "Read the third Ancient Tome.",
    [318] = "Pick up Tyr's Legacy, which the tomes lead you to; it starts A Legacy of Secrets.",
    [319] = "Tithris in the Valdrakken inn starts A Sphere in Danger with Preservationist's Dispatch Three, which points to three caves of Stormshroud Peak in Thaldraszus.",
    [320] = "In the first cave, dig up the Buried Object for a Piece of the Orb of Rathmus.",
    [321] = "Hold the Torch of Pyrreth near the hidden tablet of the first cave to reveal it, then read it.",
    [322] = "In the second cave, dig up the Buried Object for a second piece.",
    [323] = "Reveal the second cave's tablet with the Torch of Pyrreth and read it.",
    [324] = "In the third cave, dig up the Buried Object for the last piece.",
    [325] = "Reveal the third cave's tablet with the Torch of Pyrreth and read it.",
    [326] = "Fit the three pieces together into the Orb of Rathmus; it starts A Curious Orb.",
    [327] = "Bobby Carlisle in the Valdrakken inn starts They Are Always Listening; Fangli Hoot gives you the guide Great Places to Visit in Valdrakken.",
    [328] = "Find the six suspicious notes hidden around Valdrakken. Once you have all six, A Complete Inventory starts by itself.",
    [329] = "A bill of sale near the Auction House.",
    [330] = "A Void Storage receipt.",
    [331] = "A garden supply receipt.",
    [332] = "A researcher's note.",
    [333] = "A hastily scrawled note.",
    [334] = "A note to Kritha in the Dragon's Hoard, the hidden room you reach by kneeling at the Odd Statue in the Valdrakken inn.",
    [335] = "Take A Treacherous Race from Preservationist Kathos in the Valdrakken inn; she gives you the Ancient Tyrhold Artifact Notes.",
    [336] = "Light the eight orbs around Tyrhold in Thaldraszus with the Torch of Pyrreth. When the last one lights, a message says a magical lock has opened.",
    [337] = "Light the first orb.",
    [338] = "Light the second orb.",
    [339] = "Light the third orb.",
    [340] = "Light the fourth orb.",
    [341] = "Light the fifth orb.",
    [342] = "Light the sixth orb.",
    [343] = "Light the seventh orb.",
    [344] = "Light the eighth orb.",
    [345] = "At the Tyrhold Forge, walk up to Tyr's face to receive Tyr's Favor, which lasts one hour, before you hunt for the titan parts.",
    [346] = "With Tyr's Favor up, summon the Idol of Ohn'ahra on the lower rings of Tyrhold to find six titan parts in Broken Urns, fit them together, and place them in the four Titan Power Relay Consoles inside the pillars of light.",
    [347] = "Titan Cube Housing, on the top floor.",
    [348] = "Titan Energy Core, on the top floor.",
    [349] = "Titan Focusing Crystal, on the middle floor.",
    [350] = "Large Titan Capacitor, on the middle floor.",
    [351] = "A Titan Block Key Fragment, on the bottom floor.",
    [352] = "The other Titan Block Key Fragment, on the bottom floor.",
    [353] = "Combine the core and the housing into the Titan Energy Cube.",
    [354] = "Combine the two fragments into the Titan Block Key.",
    [355] = "Place the Titan Focusing Crystal in its console.",
    [356] = "Place the Titan Energy Cube in its console.",
    [357] = "Place the Large Titan Capacitor in its console.",
    [358] = "Place the Titan Block Key in its console.",
    [359] = "At the top of Tyrhold, touch the orb to start An Ominous Artifact. Defeat Amerinth and Tithris, secure the Orb of Rathmus and finish the quest.",
    [360] = "Tithris drops the Orb of Rathmus.",
    [361] = "Pick up the sealed Cache of Cosmic Curiosities beside the orb's console; the quest needs it.",
    [362] = "At the bottom of the lake below Bloodvenom Falls in Felwood.",
    [363] = "In Thousand Needles, swim in through the underwater cave by Splithoof Hold (43.9, 37.4) and follow it north to the mound.",
    [364] = "In the Eastern Plaguelands, northeast of the Plague Plaque; the Tricked-Out Thinking Cap at 15, 15 from the plaque points to it.",
    [365] = "In Shadowmoon Valley on Draenor, beside the Oracle Stone under the trees of Moonwillow Peak.",
    [366] = "Outside Manaforge B'naar in Netherstorm. Three players each hold a Torch of Pyrreth at one of the three small crystals until the mound appears.",
    [367] = "Inside the mouth of the great mogu statue in the Valley of the Four Winds.",
    [368] = "In the Azure Span a mound is hidden under one of a group of snowmen; the heat of the Torch of Pyrreth uncovers it.",
    [369] = "By the claw of the fallen dragon in the Emerald Dragonshrine of Dragonblight.",
    [370] = "In the Northern Barrens.",
    [371] = "In the Blasted Lands, find the ritual circle with a crystal in it; the Torch of Pyrreth held next to the crystal uncovers the mound.",
    [372] = "In Nagrand (Outland) the mound lies behind a skeleton on an island that floats high over Skysong Lake.",
    [373] = "In Grizzly Hills, ride the log flume of the Blue Sky Logging Grounds: Alliance players talk to Gordun (36.8, 35.7), Horde players to Darrok (35.1, 34.7). At the end the WHEE! buff lets you see the mound, at 20.2, 81.3 for the Alliance and 11.0, 74.9 for the Horde.",
    [374] = "In Dragonblight by the Bronze Dragonshrine; from the mound of rumor 8, the Tricked-Out Thinking Cap at 52, 123 leads here.",
    [375] = "Near the top of Highmountain Peak.",
    [376] = "In the middle of the Celestial Court on the Timeless Isle.",
    [377] = "In the Western Plaguelands; from the mound of rumor 3, the Tricked-Out Thinking Cap at minus 198, minus 84 leads here.",
    [378] = "On a mountain peak above Freehold in Tiragarde Sound.",
    [379] = "On Jaguero Isle off the Cape of Stranglethorn, three players with the Torch of Pyrreth light the three braziers together to call the Enigma Ward. Defeat it for the First Booster Part.",
    [380] = "In the Irontree Woods of Felwood, one player touches Mimiron's Booster Part and turns into an elemental that must envelop three other players; it then bursts and leaves the Second Booster Part.",
    [381] = "At the Dark Portal in the Blasted Lands, destroy the two Legion Flak Cannons nearby, then take Mimiron's Booster Part. Taking it takes about twelve seconds, so a friend keeping enemies off you helps.",
    [382] = "Bring all three Booster Parts to the Empowered Arcane Forge in Valdrakken and join them there; the result teaches the Mimiron's Jumpjets mount.",
    [383] = "Set one Tasty Meat down in front of the Mischievous Chick; it drops the cache key in return.",
    [384] = "The Dusty Redcap grows in the Vilaldoun cave, below Naigtal.",
    [385] = "The Partially-Digested Redcap has no patch of its own: it is one of Naigtal's drops.",
    [386] = "Feed the Sleepy Mandrake one Highland Redcap.",
    [387] = "Feed it one Dusty Redcap.",
    [388] = "Feed it one Marshy Redcap.",
    [389] = "Feed it one Partially-Digested Redcap.",
    [390] = "Feed it one Airy Redcap.",
    [391] = "With all five Redcaps eaten, the Sleepy Mandrake wakes and joins you as a pet.",
    [392] = "On the Coiled Isle, a Handful of Esoteric Ingredients starts the quest that brings you to Ofi the Sly and her cauldron.",
    [393] = "Venom-Clotted Baubles turn up at random around the island's poisoned ground; open one for a Serpent's Feather.",
    [394] = "Singing Shells turn up at random along the coasts; open one for a Clouded Blood-Pearl.",
    [395] = "Cracked Canopic Jars turn up at random around the temples; open one for an Ancient Knucklebone.",
    [396] = "On the repeatable Mixing Mysteries quest, put one Serpent's Feather, one Clouded Blood-Pearl and one Ancient Knucklebone into the cauldron: that mix gives a Balanced Offering. Other mixes give other offerings.",
    [397] = "Open the Balanced Offering; the Cauldron Concoction comes from it.",
    [398] = "In the Den, meditate at the Altar of Innocence so its spirit tells you what it lost, then pick up A Tattered Ball nearby.",
    [399] = "Bring the ball back to the Altar of Innocence and give it to the spirit.",
    [400] = "Meditate at the Altar of Wisdom, then pick up A Rolled-Up Pillow nearby.",
    [401] = "Give the pillow to the spirit at the Altar of Wisdom.",
    [402] = "Meditate at the Altar of Vigor, then pick up A Lost Hunting Knife nearby.",
    [403] = "Give the knife to the spirit at the Altar of Vigor.",
    [404] = "Once all three spirits have their things back, dive into the pool inside the Den and open the Gift of the Cycle at its bottom.",
    [405] = "Pick up the Burning Torch just left of the Triple-Locked Safebox; it shows the three hidden keys around the box.",
    [406] = "Gather 10 Bunch of Ripe Grapes from the platforms around Goldenmist Village.",
    [407] = "Put the grapes in the Stone Vat and jump around inside it until the villager by the vat says it needs yeast.",
    [408] = "Buy a Packet of Instant Yeast from Sheri, on the main platform in front of the vat.",
    [409] = "Add the yeast to the Stone Vat to finish the wine and claim the Goldenmist Grapes.",
    [410] = "Search the river below Teldrassil's burning roots, east of Har'mara and down toward the Den, for Flame-Hardened Sap of Teldrassil under the water. Each gives two to seven fragments; keep going until you have 150.",
    [411] = "Bring the 150 fragments to the Peculiar Cauldron under the bridge east of Har'mara and open it.",
    [412] = "Defeat creatures in the Maisara Deeps, around the entrance of the Maisara Caverns, for Vile Essence until you have 1000. Many of them are elite, so a group helps.",
    [413] = "Take the 1000 Vile Essence to the Abandoned Ritual Skull close to where you gathered it and open it.",
    [414] = "With a group of five, enter the Nexus-Point Xenas dungeon in Voidstorm, on any difficulty, and clear the way to Chief Corewright Kasreth.",
    [415] = "Find the five Corespark Conduits there and put one player on each. All five must step on at the same moment, so count down; standing on them hurts.",
    [416] = "A Netherstorm Structural Cage then appears on a pipe close by; open it to free Gortham.",
    [417] = "Open the Ritual Sites (the short story that starts with Ranger Captain Lilathra's Void Strike) and wait for a week when the Broken Throne in Zul'Aman is the active site. Enter it on Tier 2 or higher.",
    [418] = "Get six Practically Pork: beasts in Midnight's zones drop it, and it sells on the Auction House. Sin'dorei Swarmer, a fish from fishing pools, works in its place.",
    [419] = "In the Broken Throne, find the Lost Bear Cub on a high platform near the stairs; it is small and stealthed, and a hunter's Track Beast shows it. Feed it one Practically Pork and it becomes Chubs.",
    [420] = "Summon Chubs and go north to the pile of bones by the Chewed Meat. The Angry Amani Warbear attacks: bring it down to 1 percent health and it turns friendly.",
    [421] = "Feed the calmed warbear five Practically Pork to earn the Witherbark Warbear Mother.",
    [422] = "Open the Ritual Sites and wait for a week when Daggerspine Point, off Eversong Woods, is the active site.",
    [423] = "Defeat naga inside Daggerspine Point (Deeplurk Shadowblades, Daggerspine Infusers and Daggerspine Myrmidons) until one drops the Soggy Lynx Toy.",
    [424] = "Take the Soggy Lynx Toy to the Soggy Nest on the west side of Daggerspine Point; with it, the Void-Corrupted Snapdragon there joins you.",
    [425] = "On Sunstrider Isle, pick up the Sunstrider Vessel; Phoenix Hatchlings appear around you.",
    [426] = "Follow the hatchlings and stand in the circles they leave until you have caught five cinders, then set the vessel back where you found it.",
    [427] = "The Gift of the Phoenix then appears in front of you; open it.",
    [428] = "At the Durable Vase on the cave's upper level, mix the red and purple fluids into Fizzing Fluid. The green fluid from the Discarded Bottle is not part of the mix.",
    [429] = "In Fungara Village, pick up the Fungal Mallet; it gives you five minutes to ring the gong.",
    [430] = "Before those five minutes run out, strike the Mycelium Gong to call up the Sporespawned Cache.",
    [431] = "Find J'imothy in his arcane prison in Silvermoon City, at one of three spots. Interact to drain the prison and dodge the swirls on the floor until its Barrier Integrity is gone; other players can drain it with you to go faster.",
    [432] = "Once the barrier is down, talk to J'imothy again for the Stubby Whistle, which adds him to your pets.",
    [433] = "With a group of five, enter the Altar of Fangs on Mythic and defeat its first boss.",
    [434] = "Search the foot of the two venomous waterfalls near that boss: one player takes the Ritual Reagent bag, and each of the other four takes a Reversal Charm. They can be hard to spot.",
    [435] = "Defeat the second boss and clear the way to the Ascendant Serpent, leaving its four totems alone.",
    [436] = "Put the reagent carrier beside the Ascendant Serpent and one player at each totem. The carrier targets the serpent and uses Applying Reagent from the extra action button, then the other four use Ritual Reversal.",
    [437] = "The serpent turns into Slitherfang; talk to it to take it home as a pet.",
    [438] = "Fish in the Grisly Cod Pool for a Grisly Morsel.",
    [439] = "Feed the Grisly Morsel to the Hungry Dolphin; for the next five minutes it swims with you and points out what lies on the seabed.",
    [440] = "Dive with the dolphin and loot the Waterlogged Crate for one half of the key.",
    [441] = "Loot the Broken Urn for the other half.",
    [442] = "Open the Ritual Sites and finish one to unlock Tier 2, then wait for a week when the Broken Throne in Zul'Aman is the active site and enter it on Tier 2 or higher.",
    [443] = "Set the candle in the empty spot of the failed ritual on the platform to the right, then start the ritual.",
    [444] = "Fly your new Void-Corrupted Hex Eagle to the big pillar at the south end of the site. An updraft beside it shows only while you ride that eagle; fly into it and it carries you up to a nest.",
    [445] = "Loot the Void-Tainted Nest for the Void-Scarred Eaglet.",
    [446] = "Search the Bubbling Clams on the seabed south of the cave for a Luminescent Pearl; not every clam holds one.",
    [447] = "Carry the pearl into the cave and set it down at the marked spot; the crab Nacretta, the Pearl Hoarder, takes it and leaves a key behind.",
    [448] = "Visit the Honored Warrior's Cache inside the base of a tree west of the Temple of Akil'zon; it opens only for someone holding four tokens of the old warriors.",
    [449] = "At Jan'alai's temple, use the Honored Warrior's Urn and defeat Jan'alai's Chosen for the Dragonhawk Feather.",
    [450] = "At Nalorakk's temple, use the urn and defeat Nalorakk's Chosen for the Bear Tooth.",
    [451] = "At Akil'zon's temple, use the urn and defeat Akil'zon's Chosen for the Eagle Talon.",
    [452] = "At Halazzi's temple, use the urn and defeat Halazzi's Chosen for the Lynx Claw.",
    [453] = "With all four tokens, return to the Honored Warrior's Cache and open it.",
    [454] = "In Heroic Scholomance, the rare Doctor Theolen Krastinov sometimes appears after Rattlegore and drops the Krastinov's Bag of Horrors toy. A group member's copy works as well, so you need not own it.",
    [455] = "Defeat Darkmaster Gandling and climb to the back room of the upper floor. Use Krastinov's Bag of Horrors at the small pile of bones there, cancel its disguise, then speak with Eva Sarkhoff, who hands you an Inert Spectral Essence.",
    [456] = "Combine the Inert Spectral Essence with 5 Essence of Undeath and 3 Dark Runes to make the Spectral Essence, and equip it: Caer Darrow's ghosts and their lost things show only while you wear it.",
    [457] = "Pick up Eva's Femur from the pile of bones where Eva appeared.",
    [458] = "Find Eva's Journal tucked behind books on a shelf in the dungeon's Viewing Room.",
    [459] = "Give the Caer Darrow Fountain Water to Joseph Dirte's ghost for a Stinky Candle.",
    [460] = "Take a bucket of water from the candlelit fountain on Caer Darrow.",
    [461] = "Bring The Deed to Andorhal to Magistrate Marduke's ghost for an Authentic Andorhal Candle.",
    [462] = "The deed hangs inside Andorhal's town hall.",
    [463] = "Return the Trampled Doll to Sammy's ghost for a Ghost-Warding Candle.",
    [464] = "The doll lies by the meat wagon at Darrowshire in the Eastern Plaguelands.",
    [465] = "Show The Road Ahead to Artist Renfray's ghost for an Imported Candle.",
    [466] = "The painting hangs on the ground floor of the old inn at Corin's Crossing in the Eastern Plaguelands.",
    [467] = "Hand the Undelivered Shipment of Smokes to Rory's ghost for a Tobacco-Filled Candle.",
    [468] = "Inside Stratholme, the shipment sits on a wagon in King's Square near the broken fountain.",
    [469] = "With the five candles, Eva's Journal and her femur, enter the keep on Caer Darrow, turn right instead of going to the dungeon, and use Eva's Journal in the bone-strewn room at the far end. The ritual unlocks old Scholomance for your whole account.",
    [470] = "Read Eva's Enchanted Journal in that room to enter old Scholomance, then take the Familiar Journal from a bookshelf in its Viewing Room to learn the toy.",
    [471] = "In old Scholomance, Rattlegore's room lies below the Great Ossuary. The Cracked Argent Dawn Commission is a small item high on the bone heap in its southwest corner; a character who already owns a commission can't see it.",
    [472] = "Mend the cracked commission with 4 Truesilver Bars and a Righteous Orb, then equip the Argent Dawn Commission and keep it on for the next steps.",
    [473] = "With the commission on, clear old Scholomance to Darkmaster Gandling and take the Darkmaster's Scourgestone from him.",
    [474] = "Bring the Darkmaster's Scourgestone to Duke Nicholas Zverenhoff at Light's Hope Chapel. From then on, Scourge you defeat in Stratholme and old Scholomance can drop Invader's Scourgestones.",
    [475] = "Enter Stratholme by the main gate with the commission on and defeat the living side's Scourge until an Eye of Naxxramas shows itself; it drops the Ward of Naxxramas. Defeat no boss on the undead side yet.",
    [476] = "Take a Stratholme Holy Water from a supply crate on the living side; carry a second one for later in Naxxramas.",
    [477] = "In Crusader's Square, use the Ward to reveal the Dread Ward at the southern gate and throw the Holy Water on it. You then have five minutes to clear the undead side to Lord Aurius Rivendare and use the extra button on the Hand of Naxxramas at the gate beyond.",
    [478] = "Report to Archmage Angela Dosantos at Light's Hope Chapel.",
    [479] = "At Honored with the Argent Dawn, she asks for a Righteous Orb, 6 Large Brilliant Shards and 5 Arcane Crystals. Her quest earns the achievement and opens the Revealed Portal to Naxxramas in the north of the Eastern Plaguelands.",
    [480] = "At Revered, she asks for only 3 Large Brilliant Shards and 2 Arcane Crystals.",
    [481] = "At Exalted, she asks for nothing.",
    [482] = "Once the portal to level-60 Naxxramas is open, go to the Construct Quarter's second room and pick up the Construct's Hook lying next to a slime-filled vat.",
    [483] = "Cast a line into the slime pools of Naxxramas until an Abomination's Chain comes up.",
    [484] = "Grand Widow Faerlina in the Arachnid Quarter drops Faerlina's Sewing Kit.",
    [485] = "Put the hook, chain and sewing kit together into the Makeshift Grappling Hook; using it lets you swing between the grapple points of Naxxramas.",
    [486] = "Grapple up the ledges by the Halls of Reanimation to Zackett Skullsmash, wake him with a Stratholme Holy Water and pay his Inconvenience Fee: Black Coffee, 3 Dark Runes, 5 Corruptor's Scourgestones and 20 Invader's Scourgestones. He then trades at the heart of Naxxramas.",
    [487] = "Trade Zackett one Corruptor's Scourgestone, which Naxxramas bosses drop, for each Death's Bargaining Chip. You need 30 chips.",
    [488] = "Or trade him 10 Invader's Scourgestones, from Stratholme and old Scholomance, for each chip.",
    [489] = "Buy a Rotten Delicious from Zackett for 30 chips. Players report that a second one can't be bought after a failed try, so prepare well.",
    [490] = "Valiance, a skeletal horse, stands in the Military Quarter of the 10-player Wrath Naxxramas. While Instructor Razuvious still lives, edge up to the horse and offer the Rotten Delicious: it takes the treat, yet you still can't ride it.",
    [491] = "Use an Obedience Crystal by Razuvious to take over a Death Knight Understudy and walk it to Valiance, which accepts it as a rider. Return the rider to the boss, release it with Dismiss on its portrait, then defeat the Understudy and Razuvious for the Reins of Valiance.",
    [492] = "Join the two halves into the Restored Hakkari Bijou, which starts a quest.",
    [493] = "In Heroic Zul'Gurub, once two bosses are down, the first half lies by the gong on the ground floor of the central temple; go in by a side door.",
    [494] = "The second half appears at the same gong while Jin'do the Godbreaker's spirit phase is under way. Then break Hakkari's chains to finish the fight.",
    [495] = "Take the Restored Hakkari Bijou to Rin'wosho the Trader in Dazar'alor. The quest earns the achievement for your whole account and opens his Zandalari wares.",
    [496] = "Back in Zul'Gurub, pick up the Brazier of Madness, which stands next to the altar at the Cache of Madness site.",
    [497] = "Balakar Khan, the last boss of The Nokhud Offensive, sometimes drops a Stolen Breath of Ohn'ahra on any difficulty, Follower dungeons included. You need three.",
    [498] = "Buy an Essence of Awakening from Quartermaster Huseng in Maruukai for Dragon Isles Supplies and one Occasional Sand, which the Auction House sells or Time-Lost creatures in Thaldraszus drop.",
    [499] = "Get one Exultant Incense: alchemists make it with a recipe from Quartermaster Huseng, and it also sells on the Auction House.",
    [500] = "With all three in your bags and Maruuk Centaur renown 25, speak with Godoloto in the southern Ohn'ahran Plains for A Whispering Breeze, then fly to Ohn'ahra's Roost and hand the offerings to Ohn'ahra to learn the mount.",
    [501] = "Fish four Strange Goop out of the water where Hirukon appears in Zereth Mortis (it is a rare catch), or buy them at the Auction House: three go to the fishing spots below and one to Vashj.",
    [502] = "Speak with Vashj in Maldraxxus before you go fishing.",
    [503] = "In Zangarmarsh, spend one Strange Goop at the Pungent Blobfish Cluster inside Coilfang Reservoir to catch a Pungent Blobfish.",
    [504] = "In Nazjatar, spend one Strange Goop at the Flipper Fish School for a Flipper Fish.",
    [505] = "In the Shimmering Expanse of Vashj'ir, spend one Strange Goop at the Coilclutch Vine.",
    [506] = "Back at the Goop waters in Zereth Mortis, use the Aurelid Lure, fish in the Aurelid Cluster it creates to draw out Hirukon, and defeat it; whoever used the lure is sure to get the Deepstar Polyp.",
    [507] = "Reforge the four Quartered Ancient Rings into Nilganihmaht's Stone Ring at the Soulsteel Forge. The pieces only turn up in the week the Necrolord assault holds the Maw.",
    [508] = "Loot a Mawsworn Cache up on the ramparts of Perdition Hold; the Animated Levitating Chain gets you up there.",
    [509] = "Read the Defense Map to start \"Clearing the Walls\" and finish it for the second piece; it opens once you have done \"Putting A Plan Together\" that week.",
    [510] = "The Defense Map falls out of Mawsworn Caches around Perdition Hold once \"Putting A Plan Together\" is under way.",
    [511] = "Looting any other piece can wake the Mad Maw Construct somewhere in Perdition Hold. It runs off and vanishes within about half a minute, so be quick.",
    [512] = "After another piece is in your bags, a small container with the next piece shows up somewhere in Perdition Hold for a few minutes.",
    [513] = "Inside the Rift, defeat the rare Torglluun for Nilganihmaht's Runed Band. A Repaired Riftkey or a Collapsing Riftstone takes you into the Rift.",
    [514] = "At the Altar of Domination, use Domination's Calling to summon Exos, Herald of Domination, and defeat it for Nilganihmaht's Signet Ring. The Calling is not used up.",
    [515] = "Four players are needed to summon it; it drops the Dominion Etching: Loss.",
    [516] = "Four players are needed to summon it; it drops the Dominion Etching: Pain.",
    [517] = "Four players are needed to summon it; it drops the Dominion Etching: Grief.",
    [518] = "With four Seal Breaker Keys, unlock the Domination Sealed Chest that stands in a cage for Nilganihmaht's Silver Ring.",
    [519] = "The Harrower's Key Ring is on the wall to your right as you walk in at 66.9, 55.9.",
    [520] = "Your first Helgarde Supply Cache holds a key; later ones only hold Stygia.",
    [521] = "Ylva drops Feeder's Hand and Key; open it for a key.",
    [522] = "A Maldraxxi defector also drops a key.",
    [523] = "Start the climb at 18.6, 39.0 and work up to the summit above Calcis, where Nilganihmaht's Gold Band lies.",
    [524] = "Enter the Rift and go to the back of the cave, where the Hand of Nilganihmaht rests. Place the five rings on it one by one; the Nilganihmaht Control Ring is your reward.",
    [525] = "Day 1: find Dead Blanchy by the river in Revendreth and give her eight Handfuls of Oats.",
    [526] = "The Sacks of Oats give off no glow, so comb the field edges of the northern Westfall farms for them.",
    [527] = "Day 2: bring her a Grooming Brush.",
    [528] = "Ask Snickersnee for the Grooming Brush; you find him in Darkhaven.",
    [529] = "Day 3: bring her four Sturdy Horseshoes.",
    [530] = "Discarded Horseshoes glint along the roads of Revendreth; pick up four.",
    [531] = "Day 4: bring her a Bucket of Clean Water.",
    [532] = "Take the Empty Water Bucket that stands in Darkhaven.",
    [533] = "Fill the bucket at any river or lake in Bastion or Ardenweald.",
    [534] = "Day 5: bring her a Comfortable Saddle Blanket.",
    [535] = "Ta'tru sells the Comfortable Saddle Blanket for goods that rotate every week.",
    [536] = "Day 6: feed her three Dredhollow Apples, and her reins are yours.",
    [537] = "Mims sells the Dredhollow Apples.",
    [538] = "Every one of the six players needs the Sphere of Enlightened Cogitation learned. It comes from the Enlightened's reward caches in Zereth Mortis, so it can take a while.",
    [539] = "Team up with five other players who also have the sphere.",
    [540] = "Under the Forge of Afterlives in Zereth Mortis, six hexagonal pillars ring a pool. Each player stands on a different pillar, sits down, and all six use the Sphere of Enlightened Cogitation at the same moment.",
    [541] = "A zone-wide emote announces the Ponderer's Portal; the Enlightened Hearthstone waits inside it at the south pillar.",
    [542] = "Do the Maldraxxus world quest \"A Few Bumps Along the Way\" with a friend in a raid group to pick up two stacks of Battle Hardened; they fade after ten minutes, so the rest must follow quickly.",
    [543] = "Go to Glutharn's Decay and eat four Edible Redcap mushrooms.",
    [544] = "Hurry to the Theater of Pain, drink the Strength of Blood and the Potion of Unusual Strength so all four effects are on you together, then take Oonar's Arm from the arena.",
    [545] = "Free Mrrl: take his quest \"A Safer Place\" in Nazjatar and escort him to your faction's base, where four murloc traders join him.",
    [546] = "Take Mrrl's next quest, \"No Backs\", and buy one item from each of the four traders.",
    [547] = "Mrrglrlr trades two Pulsating Blood Stones for 16 Sea Giant Foot Dust and 14 Healthy Murloc Lunches.",
    [548] = "Grrmrlg trades the 16 Sea Giant Foot Dust for 288 Unidentified Mass (sold by Flrgrrl) and 48 Dirty Murloc Socks (sold by Hurlgrl; wash them in water first).",
    [549] = "Hurlgrl trades the 14 Healthy Murloc Lunches for 210 Slimy Naga Eyeballs (sold by Mrrglrlr) and 70 Curious Murloc Horns (sold by Grrmrlg).",
    [550] = "Mrrglrlr trades the 16 Smelly Piles of Gloop for 128 Sweet Sea Vegetables (sold by Hurlgrl) and 32 Just Regular Butter (sold by Flrgrrl).",
    [551] = "Flrgrrl trades the 28 Ghost Food for 504 Slimy Naga Eyeballs (sold by Mrrglrlr) and 168 Curious Murloc Horns (sold by Grrmrlg).",
    [552] = "When the rare Murloco event comes up, save Murloco from the naga; for five minutes afterwards he sells the Hungry Herald's Tentacle Taco for 666 gold, visible only while you wear the Azsh'ari Stormsurger Cape.",
    [553] = "Wearing the cape, check Mrrl's special stock: on the days it offers the Crimson Tidestallion, hand over four Cultist Pinky Fingers, two Pulsating Blood Stones and the taco for it.",
    [554] = "Swim through the pool into the flooded cave and take the first Damp Scroll from a skeleton's grip near the altar.",
    [555] = "The second scroll lies in a cellar north of the pool, where a K'thir Occultist keeps watch.",
    [556] = "Climb to the upper floor of the building you pass on the way to the cave for the third.",
    [557] = "The fourth waits in the cellar of the easternmost building, beside another K'thir Occultist.",
    [558] = "Crawl beneath the wooden planks of a stone building for the fifth.",
    [559] = "Return to the Ominous Altar in the cave. It asks five questions in turn; answer each with the matching line from the scrolls you read, then accept.",
    [560] = "The altar teleports you to a lonely spot well off the southern coast, with the Gem of Acquiescence in front of you; open it to learn the toy.",
    [561] = "Use the Ghostly Explorer's Skull at Frostsaber Rock in Winterspring; the ghost of Wan'be rises and tells you where he went next.",
    [562] = "Use the skull again on the floor of the Caverns of Time, just in front of Zaladormu (not up on his ledge).",
    [563] = "Use it under water in Thousand Needles, by the sunken ruins of the old raceway.",
    [564] = "Use it once more in Blackrock Mountain.",
    [565] = "Wan'be's last words send you to Nazmir, but his goods are buried on the Zuldazar side of the river: dig up the mound to get your 120 gold back.",
    [566] = "Pick up the Diary of the Night; the other four tools lie close by.",
    [567] = "Pick up the Gardener's Basket nearby.",
    [568] = "Pick up the Gardener's Flute.",
    [569] = "Pick up the Gardener's Hammer.",
    [570] = "Pick up the Gardener's Wand.",
    [571] = "Show the toolkit to Twinklestar to receive Moonsight; without that buff the chest at his back stays invisible.",
    [572] = "With Moonsight up, open the Cache of the Moon behind Twinklestar.",
    [573] = "The Raw Dream Fibers dangle from the rear edge of a raised wooden deck; take them.",
    [574] = "Look below the deck where an oversized chair stands for the Enchanted Bough.",
    [575] = "Climb to the wooden landing high in a tree for the Fae Ornament.",
    [576] = "Use the Fae Dreamcatcher on the barrier that seals the cache, then open the Cache of the Night.",
    [577] = "Hunt Glittering Grouper Brinetails in the sea off the Coiled Isle's northern tip; each one can drop a Diver's Key Fragment.",
    [578] = "Swim down to the Sunken Diver's Chest on the seabed and unlock it with the Diver's Key.",
    [579] = "Three Lost Pages lie in the southern part of Silvermoon City; this one holds the first page of the sonnets.",
    [580] = "Take the finished booklet to the Incomplete Book of Sonnets and add it there; the Silvermoon Library Bookcase is the reward.",
    [581] = "A Handful of Esoteric Ingredients, found on the Coiled Isle, starts the quest that leads you to Ofi the Sly and her cauldron.",
    [582] = "Venom-Clotted Baubles appear at random on the island's poisoned ground; each holds a Serpent's Feather. The ten mixes use ten feathers in all.",
    [583] = "Singing Shells wash up at random along the coasts; each holds a Clouded Blood-Pearl. The ten mixes use ten pearls in all.",
    [584] = "Cracked Canopic Jars appear at random near the temples; each holds an Ancient Knucklebone. The ten mixes use ten knucklebones in all.",
    [585] = "On Mixing Mysteries, drop three Clouded Blood-Pearls into the cauldron for a Choleric Offering.",
    [586] = "On Mixing Mysteries, drop one Serpent's Feather and two Clouded Blood-Pearls into the cauldron for a Virulent Offering.",
    [587] = "On Mixing Mysteries, drop two Clouded Blood-Pearls and one Ancient Knucklebone into the cauldron for a Volatile Offering.",
    [588] = "On Mixing Mysteries, drop three Serpent's Feathers into the cauldron for a Phlegmatic Offering.",
    [589] = "On Mixing Mysteries, drop two Serpent's Feathers and one Clouded Blood-Pearl into the cauldron for an Odious Offering.",
    [590] = "On Mixing Mysteries, drop two Serpent's Feathers and one Ancient Knucklebone into the cauldron for a Pestilent Offering.",
    [591] = "On Mixing Mysteries, drop three Ancient Knucklebones into the cauldron for a Melancholic Offering.",
    [592] = "On Mixing Mysteries, drop one Clouded Blood-Pearl and two Ancient Knucklebones into the cauldron for a Fragile Offering.",
    [593] = "On Mixing Mysteries, drop one Serpent's Feather and two Ancient Knucklebones into the cauldron for an Eerie Offering.",
    [594] = "On Mixing Mysteries, drop one of each ingredient into the cauldron for a Balanced Offering. Each new offering counts toward Mysterious Mix Master; the tenth earns the Mysterious Voodoo Mask.",
    [595] = "Finish one of Siren Isle's elite weekly quests, then talk to Suzie Boltwrench at Flotsam Shoal to bring the storm in; four of the five Runekeys can only be found while it rages, and it lasts until the weekly reset.",
    [596] = "During the storm, defeat Zek'ul the Shipbreaker on the southwest coast; the Cyclonic Runekey is a chance drop. It can also be fished up along that shore.",
    [597] = "During the storm, defeat Ksvir the Forgotten in the southern room of the Forgotten Vault for the Whirling Runekey.",
    [598] = "Three Turbulent Fragments join into the Turbulent Runekey.",
    [599] = "On the island's west side, a Kul Tiran ghost keeps watch over a heap of dirt during the storm; dig the fragment out of it.",
    [600] = "During the storm, a ghost in a cave north of the island's middle keeps this fragment.",
    [601] = "During the storm, a ghost in a cave in the island's southeast keeps this fragment.",
    [602] = "Seven Torrential Fragments join into the Torrential Runekey.",
    [603] = "While the storm lasts, the island's foes now and then leave a Torrential Fragment; seven make the key.",
    [604] = "Five Thunderous Fragments join into the Thunderous Runekey.",
    [605] = "Thunderous Fragments come from the hidden Runed Storm Caches that turn up during the storm, and from the Seafarer's Caches, mostly under the water, which can be opened outside it too.",
    [606] = "In the Forgotten Vault's east chamber, Thrayir sleeps among five runestones; set the Cyclonic Runekey into its stone.",
    [607] = "Set the Turbulent Runekey into its runestone beside Thrayir.",
    [608] = "Set the Whirling Runekey into its runestone beside Thrayir.",
    [609] = "Set the Torrential Runekey into its runestone beside Thrayir.",
    [610] = "Set the Thunderous Runekey into its runestone beside Thrayir.",
    [611] = "With all five stones lit, Thrayir wakes and offers the quest that gives the mount.",
    [612] = "In the Stormwind vision, with a Faceless Mask active, strike the void-touched motorcycle in the Dwarven District; Haymar the Devout comes to defend it. Defeat him, then send the wrecked frame home to Dornogal.",
    [613] = "Combine a Void-Scarred Boarhide with five Weavercloth Spellthread for the seat.",
    [614] = "The Void-Scarred Boarhide waits in the chest that appears once the Valley of Honor is cleared in the Orgrimmar vision.",
    [615] = "Combine a Magic-Lined Manifold with an Elementium-Plated Exhaust Pipe for the exhaust.",
    [616] = "The Magic-Lined Manifold sits in a crate in the Trade District of the Stormwind vision.",
    [617] = "Combine a Depleted Void Crystal, a Refulgent Crystal and Convincingly Realistic Jumper Cables for the battery.",
    [618] = "The Depleted Void Crystal waits in the chest that appears once the Mage Quarter is cleared in the Stormwind vision.",
    [619] = "Combine the Twisted Skull-Scythe Handlebars with three Whimsical Wiring, a Storm-Touched Weapon Wrap, a Recalibrated Safety Switch and an Irresistible Red Button for the handlebars.",
    [620] = "The Twisted Skull-Scythe Handlebars wait in the chest that appears once Old Town is cleared in the Stormwind vision.",
    [621] = "Combine a Void-Forged Engine Block with four Goblin-Machined Pistons for the engine.",
    [622] = "The Void-Forged Engine Block lies in the engineering shop in the Drag, in the Orgrimmar vision.",
    [623] = "Each Voidflame Wheel takes a Voidflame-Resistant Hide, Tentacle Spokes and six Entropy Enhancers; the frame needs two wheels.",
    [624] = "Voidflame-Resistant Hides turn up in the chests that appear as vision districts are cleared: the Dwarven District in Stormwind, and the Valley of Wisdom and the Valley of Spirits in Orgrimmar.",
    [625] = "Tentacle Spokes turn up in the chests that appear as vision districts are cleared: the Trade District in Stormwind, and the Drag and the Valley of Wisdom in Orgrimmar.",
    [626] = "Fit the seat onto the Deathcycle frame in the Horrific Visions hub in Dornogal.",
    [627] = "Fit the exhaust onto the frame.",
    [628] = "Fit the battery onto the frame.",
    [629] = "Fit the handlebars onto the frame.",
    [630] = "Fit the engine onto the frame.",
    [631] = "Fit both wheels onto the frame.",
    [632] = "With every part in place, press the frame's red button; the Deathcycle is yours.",
    [633] = "In the Stormwind vision's Trade District, with at least two Faceless Masks active, read the two Ripped Notes up the ramp; together they name one food and say whether it is raw or cooked.",
    [634] = "Put that one food into the Claw Marked Bowl close by and shake it. The answer changes from run to run, so bring all eight; the wrong food calls rats and the bowl is gone.",
    [635] = "The right food draws out a void-scarred gryphon; defeat it for the mount.",
    [636] = "With all three silk scraps in your bags, open the Weaving Supplies; the scraps are what unlock it.",
    [637] = "In a cave on the Isle of Dorn, talk to the one who has lost six Pearlescent Shellcrabs; you get a Crab-Guiding Branch to bring them back.",
    [638] = "Six shellcrabs are scattered across the island: at each one, use the Crab-Guiding Branch. This is the first.",
    [639] = "The sixth shellcrab is perched up in a tree; use the Crab-Guiding Branch there too.",
    [640] = "Once all six crabs are found, go back to the cave; Tree's Treasure appears beside the one who asked for help.",
    [641] = "Search the wrecked caravan here for the Battered Book.",
    [642] = "The Submerged Bottle lies in the water up by the top of the oasis falls.",
    [643] = "Climb to the top of the ruined tower and open the Ancient Coffer with the book and the bottle in your bags.",
    [644] = "Head upstairs in this building; the Well Loved Squeaky Toy is tucked away at the rear of the upper room.",
    [645] = "Find Marmaduke, who roams the middle of Siren Isle, and give the squeaky toy to the dog.",
    [646] = "Several Buried Treasure mounds are heaped up here. Dig the mound right beside the Forgotten Treasure first: it gives the Forgotten Key, and the others give only junk.",
    [647] = "Six rare makrura roam Pandaria's coasts, each carrying one clamshell. Akkalou is the first, in the Jade Forest.",
    [648] = "Kishak patrols the northern shore of Kun-Lai Summit, so he can be anywhere along it.",
    [649] = "Damlak keeps to the southern beach of Krasarang Wilds, moving between two spots.",
    [650] = "Put the six clamshells together into the Clamshell Band.",
    [651] = "On the southwest coast of Krasarang Wilds, use the Clamshell Band to call up Clawlord Kril'mandar, then defeat him; Lobstmourne almost always drops. The band is used up, so another try needs six new clamshells.",
    [652] = "While the Darkmoon Faire is in town, fish up 100 Darkmoon Daggermaw around Darkmoon Island; pools of shipwreck debris and Bloated Threshers give more at once, and they also sell on the auction house.",
    [653] = "Read the Faded Treasure Map to begin the hunt; it leads to a raft on the shore.",
    [654] = "In the tent on the beached raft, open the Barnacle-Covered Bag for a Damp Note, which points to the tigers in the sandbox.",
    [655] = "Dig in the Suspicious Mound near the sandbox tigers for a Faded Note, which points to the carnie games.",
    [656] = "Near the Faire's Careless Carnie, pick up the Crystallized Note for a Dirty Note, which points to a banner near the Faire's entrance.",
    [657] = "Dig the disturbed dirt under the banner for a Moonlit Note, which points to a sunken ship with a purple sail.",
    [658] = "Swim out to the wreck off the island's northwest coast and open the chest on the seabed; Silas' Secret Stash is inside.",
    [659] = "A Lost Mosswool has strayed onto the hills here; click it and it runs off. It shows on the minimap while you follow it.",
    [660] = "Find the Lost Mosswool again a little further south and click it once more.",
    [661] = "Click the Lost Mosswool a third time at its last stop.",
    [662] = "Where the sheep stopped for the last time, the Mosswool Flower is left behind; open it for the pet.",
    [663] = "Once you are Exalted with the Dreamweavers, buy the Seed of Solar Fire from Sylvia Hartshorn in Val'sharah for 2,000 gold.",
    [664] = "Archdruid Glaidalis, the first boss of Darkheart Thicket, can drop the Pure Drop of Shaladrassil's Sap on normal, heroic or mythic.",
    [665] = "Put the seed and the sap together into The Sunbloom, then use The Sunbloom to unlock the Sunkeeper's Reach look for the Scythe of Elune.",
    [666] = "Hyrja in the Halls of Valor can drop the Crest of the Lightborn on normal, heroic or mythic.",
    [667] = "Once you are Exalted with the Valarjar, buy the Rod of the Ascended from Valdemar Stormseeker in Stormheim for 2,000 gold.",
    [668] = "Join the crest and the rod into the Staff of the Lightborn, then use it to unlock the Crest of the Lightborn look for T'uure, the Holy priest's artifact.",
    [669] = "God-King Skovald in the Halls of Valor can drop the Haft of the God-King on normal, heroic or mythic.",
    [670] = "Nithogg, a world boss in Stormheim, can drop the Skull of Nithogg; its loot can be had once a week.",
    [671] = "Shar'thos, a world boss in Val'sharah, can drop the Skull of Shar'thos; its loot can be had once a week.",
    [672] = "Put the haft and both skulls together into The Dragonslayers, then use it to unlock the Dragonslayer's Edge look for the Warswords of the Valarjar, the Fury warrior's artifact.",
    [673] = "Start in the Netherlight Temple: talk to Archivist Inkforge and pick the middle answer each time; he hands you the fourth volume, and the rare-kill volumes only drop after this.",
    [674] = "The first volume sits on a bookshelf in Dalaran's Violet Citadel, behind the archivist there.",
    [675] = "The second volume lies on a table in an alcove of the Netherlight Temple.",
    [676] = "The third volume is on top of a bookshelf in the cloister of the New Hearthglen church in Dragonblight, on the ground floor.",
    [677] = "The fifth volume is in Scholomance, on a bookshelf in Instructor Chillheart's room; no boss kill is needed.",
    [678] = "The sixth volume is on a shelf in another alcove of the Netherlight Temple.",
    [679] = "The seventh volume is in the Scarlet Halls, by a bench in Flameweaver Koegler's room.",
    [680] = "Defeat the rare inquisitor in Stormheim for the eighth volume.",
    [681] = "Defeat the rare artificer in Suramar for the ninth volume.",
    [682] = "The tenth volume is in Black Rook Hold's library, on a table past the Amalgam of Souls.",
    [683] = "The eleventh volume is in Karazhan, past The Curator, on the low shelf of a nook below.",
    [684] = "Defeat the rare naga chief in Azsuna for the twelfth volume.",
    [685] = "Bring all twelve volumes back to Archivist Inkforge for the Writings of the End, then use it to unlock the Tomekeeper's Spire look for Light's Wrath, the Discipline priest's artifact.",
    [686] = "Demons on the Broken Isles, the Eredar of Azsuna above all, can drop the Grimoire of the First Necrolyte.",
    [687] = "Reading the grimoire starts a quest for 13 Skulls of the Executed, which only the rare elites of world quests marked as dangerous drop.",
    [688] = "Take the skulls to the Executioner's Altar in Deadwind Pass and use it.",
    [689] = "The altar calls up Sataiel; defeat him for the Essence of the Executioner, then use it to unlock the Fate's End look for Ulthalesh, the Affliction warlock's artifact.",
    [690] = "Any Eredar on the Broken Isles or Argus can drop a Damaged Eredar Head. The heads come one at a time, each only after the one before.",
    [691] = "Once the fifth head is in, Eredar can drop the Visage of the First Wakener; use it to unlock the Thal'kiel's Visage look for the Skull of the Man'ari, the Demonology warlock's artifact.",
    [692] = "As an Unholy death knight, cast Army of the Dead anywhere in the world (Apocalypse raises the same ghouls). Very rarely one of the ghouls is a special one that speaks to you and leaves Professor Putricide's Lost Journal behind; seeing it once is enough, and it opens the professor's hidden lab for you.",
    [693] = "Go to Professor Putricide's room in Icecrown Citadel: beneath its green slime pipe a trap door now opens for you. Drop through, cross the hidden lab and defeat Stitchwork at its far end for The Bonereaper's Hook, then use the hook to unlock the Bone Reaper look for Apocalypse.",
    [694] = "Any creature in Suramar can drop Candrael's Charm for a Havoc demon hunter; keep killing there until it does.",
    [695] = "Carry the charm to Candrael Twinshadow on a cliff top in western Suramar. Once you mention the initials engraved on it, she sends you over the edge, straight at Downfall.",
    [696] = "Downfall fights in midair: staying close keeps you airborne, and his blasts throw you clear now and then, so glide straight back in. Collect the Guise of the Deathwalker where he lands after the fight; it unlocks the Deathwalker look for the Twinblades of the Deceiver.",
    [697] = "At the Fel Hammer, research the order hall advancement that lets you call demons up from the Fel Tome.",
    [698] = "Take the Sanctum Crystal up to the top of the Fel Hammer and use the Fel Tome there to call a powerful demon, then defeat it. Once a day, a demon slain this way has a chance to drop the Bulwark of the Iron Warden, which unlocks the Iron Warden look for the Aldrachi Warblades.",
    [699] = "As a Retribution paladin, hand both copies of Nat Pagle's fishing guide to Sister Elda in the Sanctum of Light; she binds them into one complete copy.",
    [700] = "Players looted in Alterac Valley can drop Nat Pagle's Guide to Extreme Anglin'.",
    [701] = "The well-read copy of the guide is a book lying in Dire Maul; every wing has some.",
    [702] = "Nefarian in Blackwing Lair drops a Head of Nefarian meant for paladins.",
    [703] = "Take the head and the complete guide to Prince Tortheldrin at the end of Dire Maul West, passing the other bosses and leaving Immol'thar alone.",
    [704] = "Next speak with Alexia Ironknife at Chillwind Camp (Alliance) or Bardu Sharpeye at the Bulwark (Horde).",
    [705] = "In Hearthglen, read Grand Inquisitor Isillien's Journal.",
    [706] = "Hunt the Large Vile Slime by the Thondroril River in the Western Plaguelands for Timolain's Phylactery; it can take a long time to appear.",
    [707] = "Use the phylactery to call up Timolain the Accursed and listen to him to the end.",
    [708] = "Cast your line in the Thondroril River (its name shows under the minimap) until a Shard of Darkness bites; skill level makes no difference, and luck may ask for hundreds of casts.",
    [709] = "With the shard in your bags, speak with Lord Maxwell Tyrosus in the Sanctum of Light.",
    [710] = "He then sends you to Acherus and back; when you return to him he gives the Heart of Corruption, which unlocks the Corrupted Remembrance look for the Ashbringer.",
    [711] = "Dargrul, the last boss of Neltharion's Lair, can drop one of the two Bindings of the Windlord for a rogue of any spec, on any difficulty.",
    [712] = "Ash'Golm in the Vault of the Wardens can drop the other Bindings of the Windlord; neither drop is certain, so expect a few runs.",
    [713] = "Collect 10 Infernal Brimstone: miners gather it from Legion ore, and other players sell it.",
    [714] = "In Outlaw spec, bring both bindings and the brimstone to Thrymjaris in Stormheim and choose his second answer; the first one angers him instead.",
    [715] = "Thrymjaris then sends you to the Windlord; finish that audience to receive the Emanation of the Winds, which unlocks the Thunderfury look for the Dreadblades.",
    [716] = "As a Subtlety rogue, earn Marin Noggenfogger's Lucky Coin: Marin's order hall missions give it, and so does pickpocketing once the vault's upgrade is researched.",
    [717] = "In the Hall of Shadows, spend the coin at the vault's Sparkling Set of Keys for the Key to the Palace of Lei Shen. The vault's offers change from day to day, so the keys may not be there every day.",
    [718] = "Show the key to Taoshi in the Hall of Shadows; she sends you into the Troves of the Thunder King, a timed solo run that uses up the key.",
    [719] = "Inside, you get one Burial Trove Key when the run starts and more from chests along the way; speaking with Tenwu of the Red Smoke ends the run early with one more key.",
    [720] = "At the end, open Lei Shen's Burial Trove with a key; it can hold the Tome of Otherworldly Venoms, which unlocks the Venombite look for the Fangs of the Devourer. It is only a chance, so a run may end without it.",
